rviz_default_plugins: compute the inertia box with Eigen, not gz-math.

RViz 14 uses gz-math (gz_math_vendor) for one thing: MassMatrix3d::
EquivalentBox(), the box shown for a link's inertia. gz-math and the
gz-cmake/gz-utils it needs are not part of this tree's ROS 2; the same
computation (the inertia tensor's principal moments and axes, and the
uniform-density box with those moments) is a few lines of Eigen, which RViz
already depends on.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [gz-math is available on RViz's platforms]
